boot: stzos init -- machine qemu_confine (hosted / x86_64 / qemu_pc) -- pid 1
boot: console /dev/ttyS0
boot: mount proc at /proc -- done
boot: mount sysfs at /sys -- done
boot: mount devtmpfs at /dev -- done
boot: grant process (effectful)
boot: grant network (effectful)
boot: grant filesystem (effectful)
boot: network lan -- eth0 up 10.0.2.15/24, gateway 10.0.2.2 (dhcp), dns [10.0.2.3], /etc/resolv.conf written
boot: confine -- sealed has no network of its own, still has no way to start another process; what a world did not declare, the kernel does not give it
boot: start sealed -- pid N -- /stzos confined eth0
confined: eth0 -- no such interface from here: this world has a network namespace of its own and there is nothing in it
confined: fork -- permitted: this world started another process, and this line is the child speaking
boot: sealed (pid N) exited 0
boot: start still -- pid N -- /stzos confined eth0
confined: eth0 -- present: this world shares the machine's network
confined: fork -- refused by the kernel (EPERM): this world cannot start another process
boot: still (pid N) exited 0
boot: start open -- pid N -- /stzos confined eth0
confined: eth0 -- present: this world shares the machine's network
confined: fork -- permitted: this world started another process, and this line is the child speaking
boot: open (pid N) exited 0
boot: judge -- the boot matches its expectation (/etc/expected, 16 lines)
boot: every service has ended -- init has nothing left to keep alive
boot: init halts the machine -- reboot(RESTART)
reboot: Restarting system
